KiCad library snapshots
=======================

Study.kicad_sym and the standard footprints copied into Study.pretty derive
from the KiCad libraries installed with KiCad 10.0.6. Source identifiers are
recorded in design.py. Library sources:
https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries/kicad-symbols
https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries/kicad-footprints
https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries/kicad-packages3D

KiCad libraries are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 with the KiCad library
exception. The exception permits unrestricted use of library data in
electronic designs and their manufacture. KICAD-LICENSE.txt retains the
upstream license/exception notice. See the upstream LICENSE.md files:
https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries/kicad-symbols/-/blob/master/LICENSE.md
https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries/kicad-footprints/-/blob/master/LICENSE.md

Project symbol aliases, hidden sourcing fields and blanked upstream footprint
filters are modifications. The ESP32 footprint uses 0.30mm thermal-pad holes;
its clipped pin marker is on Fab. The USB footprint references a local nominal
envelope because the installed library has no matching STEP model.
TESwitch, PogoPads and LCDPads are project-created footprints. Their geometry
and the local nominal switch/USB STEP models are not manufacturer CAD models.

Manufacturer documents remain copyrighted by their respective owners. They
were consulted, not redistributed. Part selections and sources are in the
BOMs and reports/sources.json. No endorsement is implied. Other
